1. Henri Poincaré, [“Sur la dynamique de l'électron,” June 5, 1905, original scan](https://www.academie-sciences.fr/pdf/dossiers/Poincare/Poincare_pdf/Poincare_CR1905.pdf), with the [readable English translation](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Translation:On_the_Dynamics_of_the_Electron_(June)); Albert Einstein, [“On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies,” June 30, 1905](https://www.fourmilab.ch/etexts/einstein/specrel/www/). See [S67](sources.md#s67). The comparison establishes proximity and overlapping problems, not identical theories or complete independence.

2. Einstein, [1905 paper](https://www.fourmilab.ch/etexts/einstein/specrel/www/), opening and section 1. The maps and probability model are original explanatory illustrations. No claim is made to derive relativity from an entropy-production calculation.

3. David H. Wolpert and William G. Macready, [“No Free Lunch Theorems for Optimization”](https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~hutter/earg/papers07/00585893.pdf) (1997). The equal-average result has specified finite-search and averaging assumptions; it does not say that useful biases are unavailable in real problems. Its use here identifies a question about historically acquired search structure. See [S127](sources.md#s127).

4. **Dialectical vocabulary and the book’s interpretation.** Friedrich Engels, [*Dialectics of Nature*, II: “Dialectics”](https://www.marxists.org/archive/marx/works/1883/don/ch02.htm), lists the three formulations discussed here. Their proposed grounding in ontological uncertainty belongs to this manuscript. The wave–particle reading is not attributed to Einstein as a declared dialectical method. A physical threshold or a revision of categories alone does not identify that ontology. See [S130](sources.md#s130).

5. Einstein, [1909 radiation lecture, English translation](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Translation:The_Development_of_Our_Views_on_the_Composition_and_Essence_of_Radiation). See [S65](sources.md#s65). The dialectical reading belongs to this book. The chapter separates light, later matter-wave developments, and relativity; no invented quotation or Hegelian self-description is attributed to Einstein.

6. **Empirical research design (S111).** Unexpected deaths of leading scientists and collaborators' output. Interrupting an established knowledge network changes what its surviving members can produce. The [chapter-specific specification](scripts/experiments.json) and [research guide](scripts/README.md) document the comparison, assumptions, and limits; the [run report](scripts/results/chapter04.json) records the actual data status. This component test does not by itself establish the chapter's broader synthesis.
